{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the woman saw.</b> She saw the words of the serpent and they pleased her, and she believed them (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>That the tree was good.</b> To become like Elohim." "<b>And that it was a desire to the eyes.</b> As he said to her: ״וְנִפְקְחוּ עֵינֵיכֶם״." "<b>And that the tree was to be desired to make one wise.</b> As he said to her: ״יֹדְעֵי טוֹב וָרָע״." "<b>And she gave also to her husband.</b> Lest she die and he live, and he marry another." "<b>Also.</b> To include beast and wild animal."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:23.625210450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}